Claim NMD-C-24-2207 is closed. Closure notice attached.<br />
<br />
Indemnity paid: none. The indemnity reserve is fully released. For the reco=
rd it went from the $2,150,000 I set at the demand, to $250,000 on January =
8 once I had read the May 17 directive, to zero on February 24 after the wi=
thdrawal. Total defense cost was $61,400, all incurred between November 21 =
and February 21, and it is not chargeable to your loss experience because t=
he claim resolved without payment.<br />
<br />
Priscilla, for what it is worth from the carrier side. We see roughly forty=
 of these a year and the ones that go badly are almost never about the desi=
gn. They are about a firm that made the right call in year one and cannot p=
rove it in year fourteen. Your firm kept its mail. That is the whole differ=
ence between a closed file and a seven figure check.
